    {
      "id": "1222404199",
      "uuid": "1d9a4db3-399c-4ed1-a57c-4c212f4d2907",
      "file_key": "cCmVBQQfWKd3I9rgaUqOLo",
      "parent_id": "",
      "user": {
        "handle": "Emily Wachowiak",
        "img_url": "https://s3-alpha.figma.com/profile/573cff47-057f-45b9-9013-0d6d20d59e69",
        "id": "1108498254843026326"
      },
      "created_at": "2025-04-17T19:15:34.897Z",
      "resolved_at": null,
      "message": "A few things based on the way Edge handles this:\n1. They let you set default profiles for external links or even certain websites. \n2. Interestingly, the last used profile always opens at startup and there is no setting for this. \n3. They have \"Last used (default)\" as an option to pick from\n\nHow this applies to us:\n1. The user story is just about app startup, but do we also want it to apply to external links as well?\n2. Do we think we'll ever want to get more granular and add custom sites/apps as well? If so I can think more scalably about the name.\n3. I think we should have a last used option and potentially make that the default option.\n4. I think we should provide a path to get to these settings from the Profile Manager, and potentially a way to note the default profile on the manager (we might not want to do this if we get more granular in the future though)\n@Misha Bruk",
      "reactions": [],
